WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.240
Matt Reeves' "The Batman" is everywhere right&nbsp;
now. The first Batman solo movie in 10 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.200
made more than $164 million at the American box&nbsp;
office just six days into its theatrical run,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.280
and according to Box Office Mojo, it's already&nbsp;
the second-highest-grossing film of 2022.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.160
In "The Batman," Robert Pattinson's Batman has&nbsp;
been patrolling Gotham City's streets at night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.880
for nearly two years with little to show for&nbsp;
it. His fledgling partnership with police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.600
lieutenant James Gordon leaves the two at odds&nbsp;
with the rest of the city's power structure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.280
and it all comes to head when the Riddler&nbsp;
starts killing Gotham politicians.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.680
Paul Dano's depiction of the Riddler was the&nbsp;
first time the character appears in big-screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:47.920
live-action Batman content since Jim Carrey&nbsp;
played the role in 1995's "Batman Forever."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.760
It's a distinctly different approach;&nbsp;
Dano's character appears much more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.560
like a villain in a serial killer movie&nbsp;
than Carrey's loud, bombastic trickster.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.880
"The Batman" also includes villains&nbsp;
The Penguin and Carmine Falcone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.680
but perhaps the most intriguing villain is one&nbsp;
who makes only an uncredited cameo appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.160
at the end of the film. Spoilers ahead!

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:14.400
Barry Keoghan of "Eternals" and "The Killing of&nbsp;
a Sacred Deer" fame is only credited as "Unseen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.120
Arkham Prisoner" in "The Batman," but when he&nbsp;
appears imprisoned alongside the Riddler at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.480
the end of the movie, nobody could mistake&nbsp;
him for Batman's arch-nemesis, the Joker.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.520
Reeves attempts to set up a litany of Batman&nbsp;
villains for his burgeoning cinematic universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.200
In fact, a deleted scene reportedly shows Batman&nbsp;
visiting Keoghan in prison to get a profile on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.400
the Riddler, which has fans wondering what the&nbsp;
actor would be like as the clown prince of crime.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.760
While Reeves has said these villains&nbsp;
are in their infancy in "The Batman,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.600
it seems pretty clear Keoghan's&nbsp;
character will take on the Joker title&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.200
in whatever future sequel awaits&nbsp;
Robert Pattinson's Batman.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.560
In the meantime, fans like&nbsp;
Instagram user arifinity_&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.760
are offering up sample art of what Keoghan's Joker&nbsp;
could look like with green hair, clown makeup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.960
and an exaggerated red smile. Behind&nbsp;
Keoghan's Joker is graffiti similar to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:10.480
is seen in "The Batman," but Joker-themed.&nbsp;
Keoghan's prison jumpsuit sports the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.720
"Joe," although it's unclear what&nbsp;
Reeves' Joker's real name is, as of yet.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:20.080
Reeves told IGN that his conception of Keoghan's&nbsp;
pre-Joker stage involves the character having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.440
condition that makes it impossible for him to stop&nbsp;
smiling, making his Joker title a reflection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.480
having lived life as a "cruel joke." However,&nbsp;
the director stressed that Keoghan's inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:36.560
is not necessarily meant to tease the Joker as&nbsp;
a villain for his next movie. Reeves told IGN,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.160
"I don't know that the Joker would be&nbsp;
in the next movie, but I can tell you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:43.760
that here's what you're seeing, is an&nbsp;
early days version of this character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.880
and trouble, as always, is brewing in Gotham."

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.120
For the most part, fans are liking the&nbsp;
potential they see in a new kind of Joker.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.120
Instagram user arifinity_ said they&nbsp;
enjoyed "The Batman" in the Instagram&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.280
post containing their interpretation&nbsp;
of how Keoghan's Joker could look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.480
complimenting the film's portrayal of Batman&nbsp;
as a detective, and the effects, posting,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:10.320
"The visuals were stunning and most of it looked&nbsp;
practical, which I appreciate. Cast chemistry was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:16.960
great, Paul Dano was probably my favorite out of&nbsp;
the cast. That one scene (iykyk) was exceptional."

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:22.160
Reactions to the user's Joker fan art, which&nbsp;
positions the right half of Pattinson's Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.880
opposite the left half of Keoghan as the&nbsp;
Joker, emphasizing the yin-yang nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.000
their relationship, appear positive. Plenty&nbsp;
of users left fire emojis in the comments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.320
of the post, and the word "epic"&nbsp;
was tossed around. One user wrote,

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.720
"Love this. I wasn't so sure of Barry&nbsp;
playing the Joker but when I saw it...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.480
HIS LAUGH STOLE THE SHOW."

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.160
Audiences don't see much of&nbsp;
Keoghan at all in his one scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.240
but once his character establishes a&nbsp;
budding friendship with Dano's Riddler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.960
that unmistakable laugh signals plenty of&nbsp;
trouble ahead for Pattinson's Bruce Wayne.

